 ('prize','Squid Game and derivative television','Leiden Arts in Society contributor','https://www.leidenartsinsocietyblog.nl/articles/squid-game-and-the-significance-of-derivative-television','secondary_criticism','The Prize of Peril concerns a marginalized hard worker risking his life for wealth.','This does not support the discovery guess of a public automated income floor; adaptations have separate premises.'),
 ('tranai','A Ticket to Tranai, bounded factory passage','Robert Sheckley text reproduced by RuLit','https://www.rulit.me/books/a-ticket-to-tranai-read-318850-11.html','bounded_primary_passage','Goodman takes a robot-factory engineering job and tests deliberately sluggish household robots.','One short factory passage only; no universal household entitlement or employment-preservation motive established.'),
 ('ophiuchi','The Ophiuchi Hotline','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Ophiuchi_Hotline','secondary_plot_reference','Varied Eight Worlds, advanced biological techniques and an AI-governed Luna coexist.','Not one verified uniform access system; Steel Beach is not silently imported as this novel’s exact chronology.'),
 ('steel','Steel Beach','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steel_Beach','secondary_plot_reference','Central Computer governs citizens’ lives, provides ongoing services and later carries out coercive experiments.','The established support phase is separated from later failures, hidden groups and unreliable narration.'),
