R=[scoped_record('c0803','steel-beach-luna-central-computer','Steel Beach — Luna under the Central Computer','Steel Beach','Computer-governed lunar provision before the later crisis',['book'],
 'Steel Beach novel-specific Eight Worlds variant','Established Central Computer support before the later raids and acute malfunction','Living human and active human-derived lunar citizens',
 ['Every Eight Worlds novel as an identical timeline','Hidden independent surface groups','Inactive personality recordings as supported active residents'],
 'Luna’s Central Computer maintains the society in which oxygen, food, water and medical intervention are routinely provided. The setting separates material support from a person’s immediate success at paid employment, while still supplying jobs and occasions for purposeful activity. Guarantees are rated strong within the established order, with qualifications about coercive intervention and the later computer crisis. A life-support floor is not an assertion that every personal preference is respected.\n\nThe Computer is government, court, information source and intimate adviser, placing authority near autonomous AI control. Human occupations and preferences do not establish a right to overrule that system. Journalism, ranching, care and recreational construction can all be useful work, so the comfortable economy provides no reliable nonworking census. The point concerns this novel’s implemented Luna rather than importing its institutions backward into every Eight Worlds story. Active human-derived people are an explicit proxy where relevant; stored recordings and the hidden surface community are outside this provision scope.',
 [-.75,-.95,None],[[-.95,-.15],[-1,-.75],None],
 ['The review explicitly lists society-provided oxygen, food, water and medical care; the setting reference identifies the controlling machine system.','The Central Computer governs and adjudicates ordinary life; its assistance is not human collective ownership.',nw],refs,5,proxy=True)]
refs=[P+'aristoi-author',P+'aristoi']
R.append(scoped_record('c0806','aristoi-logarchy-demos','Aristoi — The Logarchy’s supported Demos','Aristoi','Ordinary citizens under nanotechnological Aristoi rule',['book'],
 'Walter Jon Williams’s Aristoi setting','Established reconstructed Logarchy before the secret-world conflict','Living human Demos in functioning Logarchy domains',
 ['The hidden involuntary experimental world','Each daimone as an extra independent citizen','Equal access to rulers’ nanotechnology inferred from exams'],
 'The Logarchy’s nanotechnology supports a comfortable ordinary population with serious illnesses eliminated and injuries repairable. The author explicitly frames the setting as post-scarcity, while the detailed reference connects its productive capabilities to a specialized ruling class. Guarantees receive a strong but qualified estimate within the established domains: routine material ease and healing are clear, while individual rulers can shape local conditions and residents do not possess the same powers.\n\nOnly the Aristoi are authorized to develop and use the decisive nanotechnology. They govern their domains, making control highly concentrated in human and human-derived elites rather than common ownership or external AI sovereignty. Competitive examinations permit movement within the hierarchy but do not grant everyone equal authority over production. The rulers’ divided mental subselves are not multiplied into a population of independent nonworkers. Ordinary and elite residents can still create, study, govern and care for others; post-scarcity alone does not establish that no useful work remains, so participation stays unresolved.',
 [-.7,0,None],[[-.95,-.1],[0,.15],None],
 ['Author-described post-scarcity is tied to controlled nanotechnology, ordinary comfort and comprehensive healing in the detailed setting reference.','Human/human-derived Aristoi monopolize authorized use of the decisive productive technology.',nw],refs,1))
refs=[P+'spaces',P+'spaces-jacket',P+'spaces-reader']
R.append(scoped_record('c0807','implied-spaces-constructed-worlds','Implied Spaces — The supported constructed-world civilization','Implied Spaces','The established human communities supported by pocket-universe infrastructure',['book'],
 'Walter Jon Williams’s original novel setting','Established civilization before Vindex’s resurrection sabotage and war','Living humans and active human-derived residents of functioning constructed worlds',
 ['Deliberately chosen fantasy scarcity as universal deprivation','Dormant backups as active beneficiaries','Every pocket universe as having identical local government'],
 'Constructed pocket universes and their sustaining supercomputers provide the setting for a civilization explicitly described by the gathered reader account as post-scarcity. Designer embodiment, resurrection and the ability to inhabit elaborately built worlds are implemented features, not merely a proposal to upload someday. Guarantees are provisionally favorable for functioning communities, with a broad allowance for unequal local arrangements and vulnerability of the underlying infrastructure. Chosen fantasy-world hardship is not assigned to all residents.\n\nControl remains unresolved. Human political institutions coexist with indispensable supercomputers, and infrastructure dependence alone does not prove that those machines are independent sovereigns. The later corruption and resurrection attacks demonstrate an important failure mode, but are outside the earlier support score. Humans and active human-derived residents form the explicit population proxy; backups are excluded. Exploration, art, research and infrastructure work continue, so neither extended life nor constructed worlds supplies a nonworking percentage. Publisher and plot context support the mechanism while the post-scarcity interpretation remains honestly labeled as secondary.',
 [-.65,None,None],[[-.95,.25],None,None],
 ['Maintained constructed worlds and implemented resurrection/embodiment support the reader’s explicitly post-scarcity interpretation, qualified by local variation and substrate dependence.','Human governments and indispensable supercomputers coexist without a clearly verified ultimate productive-control rule.',nw],refs,1,proxy=True,alternatives=[5]))
refs=[P+'torch']
R.append(scoped_record('c0808','riding-torch-convoy-abundance','Riding the Torch — The abundant refugee convoy','Riding the Torch','The matter-energy supplied human torchship population',['short_story'],
 'Norman Spinrad’s novella as described in the bounded reader plot account','Established centuries-long convoy life before the scout revelation','Living human inhabitants of the refugee torchship convoy',
 ['The Council’s navigation powers as proof of ownership of every personal fabricator','Artists and pilots as doing no useful work','A collective search for a planet as present material starvation'],
 'The refugee convoy can manipulate matter and energy to shape living environments, meals and experiences while traveling between stars. Most residents enjoy a continuing culture of sensory art, parties and leisure rather than earning ordinary subsistence through production jobs. Guarantees receive a favorable estimate for that functioning technological support. The evidence is a clearly labeled reader plot account, so enforceable civic rights and the exact limits of provision remain uncertain.\n\nA Council of Pilots coordinates the search for a habitable destination, while individuals can reshape their own surroundings. Navigation authority does not by itself establish centralized ownership of production, nor does personal access prove equal command of the entire infrastructure; control stays unresolved. A high, broad nonworking estimate follows the extensive leisure description, with substantial room for pilots, artists, care, maintenance and useful creative work. It is not a canonical census. The failure to find a new home is not confused with immediate inability to provide necessities aboard the existing convoy.',
 [-.7,None,.75],[[-.95,.15],None,[.35,.95]],
 ['The specific plot review describes actual matter-energy manipulation, food/experience creation and continuing leisure for most convoy residents.','Council navigation and individual environmental creation do not establish one effective productive-ownership model.','Extensive leisure supports .75 [.35,.95] as a broad editorial estimate; artists, pilots and other useful contributors still count.'],refs,1,alternatives=[2]))

